WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:15.540
Giuse-san. Have you picked
out a souvenir for Henrietta?

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:18.680
I'm not sure what to choose.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.980
It's tough, because she
loves anything I give her...

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.190
You have it easy, Hirscher,
always buying stuffed animals.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.060
You don't get it, do you?

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:31.390
Triela is always
researching what she wants,

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.990
so I can't choose just anything.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.030
Incidentally, what I got her
this time is called a Steiff bear...

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.270
Your souvenir from France is a Steiff?

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:43.710
Excuse me.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.340
I take it you're from Italy?

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.980
Yeah. We're on our way
home from a business trip.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:51.910
We're just about to take the train.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:56.380
If it's a French souvenir
you're wanting, I can help you out.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:58.350
Do you have anything good?

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:04.460
It's for this "Henriette" girl, yes?
Then I got just the thing.

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:07.290
It's even got a great story to it...

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:36.120
Is it true you're going to
the Balkans, Giuse-niisama?

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.060
It'll only be for half a year.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:44.400
Don't go! They say it's
dangerous because of the radiation!

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:48.400
You won't be lonely.
Our brother will still be here.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:54.610
But... Jean-niisama
never comes to my recitals.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:57.310
Yes, Jean-san.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.750
Our meeting with the French
Ministry of the Interior ended fine.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:03.380
We're heading back on the TGV now.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:06.720
There's going to be a large-scale
demonstration in Rome tomorrow.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:08.520
Try to be back in time.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.460
Understood.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:23.170
Amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:38.190
I want to protect you and fulfill
my promise to the only one for me

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:45.760
In a world filled with doubt,
I still can't find the answer

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:52.870
Even so, I continue forward... Why?

00:02:52.870 --> 00:03:03.480
If I can change this dream-like
reality with my own two hands,

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:10.790
amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:18.430
I want to protect the only one for me

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:26.070
I swear on my beating heart I will
continue to run until I burn away

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:33.740
Amid the eternal love
I feel simply by living,

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:42.910
I want to fulfill my promise

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:02.160
"Italy Social Welfare Agency
Engineering Wing"

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.110
I'll see you later!

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:18.360
"Distance Between Two: Brother and Sister"

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:23.420
"Rome, Italy"

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:14.240
Giuse. The activists don't appear
to be doing anything at the moment.

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:18.340
Yeah, they don't, Brother.

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:30.520
This is my brother.
But we're not real siblings.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:34.160
We're always together during missions,

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:39.030
so we're called a
"fratello... brother and sister."

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:42.070
Close, but not close enough to touch.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.100
That's how far apart Giuse-san and I are.

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:50.300
I'd like to get closer to him, though...

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:55.980
Rico. Use the sidewalk.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:10.930
Henrietta.

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:11.900
Something the matter?

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:14.930
No! It's nothing!

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:33.620
"Roman Coliseum"

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:32.080
Sir.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:37.120
A serious clash has broken out
between the protestors and the MPs.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:42.820
This is it. It's very likely
they'll use this as a chance to strike.

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:44.990
Where are the fratellos?

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:48.760
Jean-Rico and Guise-Etta
teams are heading north

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:51.130
from Circo Massimo Station.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:56.090
Hirscher-Triela team is watching
from the Memorial Observatory.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:02.510
The other members are patrolling
the area for anyone suspicious.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:07.740
Contact the Handlers.
Tell them to find the F.R.F. Terrorists.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:14.590
"San Gregorio Street, Rome"

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:21.960
Giuse. We're going to return
to the chief's van real quick.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.530
You stay here and watch the perimeter.

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.060
Got it.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:35.210
Is that the Five Republics
Faction causing all that?

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.080
Those are ordinary citizens.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:40.100
Even in Rome, there are lots
of pro-independence supporters.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:04.570
Are you okay, Giuse-san?!

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:11.030
You're bleeding!

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:19.320
It's only a scratch.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:21.810
More importantly,
we need to watch the perimeter!

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:30.720
Look!

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:38.270
Let's go!

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.380
Priscilla!

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:51.590
Giuse-san! Etta!
What was that explosion?!

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:54.120
Padania terrorists! Let me borrow this!

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.620
O-Okay.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.290
Alright! Get on!

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.760
Yes, sir!

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:20.850
My Vespa... I hope I get it back...

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:41.770
I did it! I killed 10 guys!
All thanks to this!

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:44.640
These bombs are incredible.

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.980
Now we can get up close without
the police dogs detecting them.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:51.710
When we get the chance,
we'll blow another two or three elsewhere.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.010
Hey, doesn't that scooter seem strange?!

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:24.880
It's been following us for a while now!

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:30.280
Wait. There's too much traffic here.

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:33.380
The place'll be swarming with
cop cars if we cause a scene, too.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.930
Giuse-san! I see a
Beretta submachine gun!

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:42.000
Not yet!

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:43.960
Giuse! Do you read me?!

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.800
The administrative district is coming up.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:49.630
We'll corner the target up ahead!

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:52.740
Got it!

00:11:52.740 --> 00:11:56.740
Rico. We're going to get ahead of
them and cut off their escape route.

00:11:56.740 --> 00:11:58.610
Yes, Jean-san!

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:00.510
Do we kill them?

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:06.950
No, we need someone to
interrogate. Just make them hurt.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.220
Yes, sir!

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:19.930
Damn it!

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:44.020
It looks like we can lead the
enemy's car into this narrow alleyway.

00:12:44.020 --> 00:12:45.550
Yes.

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:49.400
Let's use this to set a trap.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:52.020
Yes. That's a good idea.

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:39.280
You all right, Henrietta?

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:42.480
Yes. I'm fine.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:54.060
Shit!

00:14:39.240 --> 00:14:41.740
Is that good?

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:43.970
Yeah. That'll do.

00:14:50.620 --> 00:14:51.950
Don't go anywhere!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.610
I'm going to make you regret
everything soon enough!

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:05.660
Damn you!

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:16.180
Several years ago,

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:20.480
this country's prime minister
founded the Social Welfare Agency,

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:23.920
a public-interest organization
intended to perform charity work.

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:27.590
In truth, it's an intelligence
agency that covertly removes

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:30.610
those who oppose the government.

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:35.230
Triela! Are you all right?

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:40.300
Within the agency,
our Special Ops Section 2

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:44.370
gathers patients around
the country on the verge of death,

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:47.670
gives them mechanical bodies,
and sends them on dangerous missions.

00:15:54.420 --> 00:15:55.720
Using what's called "conditioning,"

00:15:55.720 --> 00:16:01.590
the girls have their memories of
their previous lives blocked out,

00:16:01.590 --> 00:16:06.320
and are made to obey the orders
of their partners and the agency.

00:16:08.030 --> 00:16:12.760
The powerful bodies they're
given allow them to survive,

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:18.860
but in exchange, they lose
their pasts and free will.

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:32.620
These "cyborgs" can kill
without any hesitation whatsoever.

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:09.920
"Today, I killed an enemy for Giuse-san."

00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:13.660
"I'm sad I wasn't very helpful,

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:18.150
but I was happy when he
held me on the scooter!"

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:24.400
The end.

00:18:04.380 --> 00:18:07.640
Giuse-san. It's me, Henrietta.

00:18:32.840 --> 00:18:34.770
It smells like cigarettes...

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:39.140
Did Giuse-san have a cigarette?

00:19:45.780 --> 00:19:49.810
Could this be my souvenir from France?

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:17.870
A gold kaleidoscope...

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:27.380
It's written in French.

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:34.320
"For my beloved,
Louise Antoinette Rolle..."?

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:12.930
I-I'm sorry!

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.830
Henrietta...

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.670
I don't know...

00:21:18.670 --> 00:21:23.170
A kaleidoscope that's
addressed to a woman as a present...

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:32.720
Say, Henrietta. What was
this woman's name again?

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:36.880
Umm, Louise Antoinette Rolle...

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:41.900
I guess it really is Giuse-san's girlfriend?

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:45.730
I wouldn't worry.
She died in the 19th century.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:47.030
Eh?

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:49.840
Unless it's a case of
someone with the same name,

00:21:49.840 --> 00:21:54.940
that's the name of a married woman
a great French writer once loved.

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:59.850
He wrote a love story based
on himself and Mrs. Rolle,

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:03.620
but the heroine in that
novel was named Henrietta.

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:05.950
- Oh...
- Then...

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:09.460
The present was for you.

00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:13.390
As thoughtful and roundabout as it was.

00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:32.980
Umm! Uhh! I, uhh...

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:42.720
Uranus rotates horizontally, almost
along the same path as its orbit.

00:22:42.720 --> 00:22:48.100
So its rings look
especially round from Earth.

00:22:48.100 --> 00:22:53.060
There are some small moons
nearby called "shepherd moons."

00:22:54.070 --> 00:22:55.600
They're called that because...

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:57.370
Say, Claes.

00:22:57.370 --> 00:23:00.670
What? Let me sleep...

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:04.340
Was that novel about
a love that succeeded?

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:05.680
No.

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:08.750
Is it okay that her
present has bad luck, then?

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:12.590
She'll be okay.
It's probably a fake anyway.

00:23:12.590 --> 00:23:17.190
After all, kaleidoscopes
had just been invented then.

00:23:17.190 --> 00:23:19.390
Ah.

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:22.530
Besides, if love doesn't
work out in a story like that,

00:23:22.530 --> 00:23:25.470
it wasn't true love to begin with.

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:28.100
Have I answered all
your questions, Triela-kun?

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:30.260
Yes, Claes-sensei!

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:58.700
A doll without a heart,
born from warm hands

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:08.210
I neither smile nor talk

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:16.220
I want you to hear about
these feelings someday,

00:24:16.220 --> 00:24:24.260
though they can't be put into words

00:24:24.260 --> 00:24:32.530
I'll summon all my strength

00:24:32.530 --> 00:24:44.910
to know what it means to live

00:25:01.630 --> 00:25:06.530
"Pinocchio"
